CFX confirmed they need PGP key 925B09E785B78FF4 to decrypt — but my script is only ever producing 4E25745981D458FB. I traced this down and found the two are actually the same keypair — 925B09E785B78FF4 is the encryption subkey, 4E25745981D458FB is the primary key. The script's logic on line 62 just grabs whichever key is listed first in the keyring (gpg --list-keys --with-colons | awk -F: '/^pub:/ ... {print $5; exit}') and always pulls the primary key ID — it has no vendor-aware or subkey-aware logic at all. It happens to have been working for other interventions purely by coincidence of keyring ordering, not by design.


